  message: "P2 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 24d0b860ee; owner-requested re-check of the 51 open P2 violated/todo_hard/todo_soft items; fixtures and outputs under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p2_review_11012026/B1/). VERDICT: CURRENT, with a non-discriminating DONE WHEN. Fixture: host-secret-no-network reads violated for BOTH init_local and control, but init_local's flow is analysis_method ddg_mixed / approximate / walk_verdict escaped (call-graph reachability, source and sink in one function) while control is ddg / precise / reached; -logging and -host-fs are inconclusive: 'leaves through 1 construct(s) the taint walk does not follow (out_parameter_call at main.c:13)' (c.py:533-539 stamp; taint.find_unfollowed_escapes taint.py:4718-4792). So the item's 'DONE WHEN ... in the SAME function reads violated' is already met today by reachability. Real criterion: the init_local flow reports walk_verdict reached (precise) and no out_parameter_call escape is disclosed at main.c:13. INV-nohob satisfied 10-19 (disclosure PRs #1740/#1741). MECHANISM: the 3a DDG walk is intraprocedural and memory-agnostic; a callee's write through a pointer parameter produces no def of the caller's argument. ROOT-CAUSE GROUP: taint walk cannot cross memory it does not own (with WI-zitul; WI-potan is the Go summary-model twin: no param_to_param). Status unchanged."  # 4db4
